Convective Heat Transfer — Arup Kumar Das (@th-das: 0, is #reference, #part-of @th-sources) { r_1BYB2QY61ENBK9WGCHBBC5YE92
Arup Kumar Das, IIT Roorkee. NPTEL 112107211. [Course](https://nptel.ac.in/courses/112107211) · [Four-week syllabus](https://archive.nptel.ac.in/content/syllabus_pdf/112107211.pdf) · [Archived teaching context](https://onlinecourses-archive.nptel.ac.in/noc17_me05/preview).

Complete the derivation/tutorial sequence: thermal energy balance, low/high-Prandtl external layers, constant-flux/temperature walls, natural convection, internal and developing duct transport, Rayleigh–Bénard behavior, phase change and mass-transfer analogy. Check the geometry, thermal boundary condition and regime behind each expression.

This four-week elective is a focused analytical companion, not a replacement for a complete first heat-transfer book or the later graduate investigations. Distinguish archived run dates from the course identifier. Public viewing and the licences of individual materials are separate questions; source materials stay external.

